  "caveats": [
    "Revenue is an estimate: declared price x Coinbase's own l30DaysTotalCalls, not an independently measured settlement count.",
    "Declared price matched charged price in 37 of 38 classifiable probes, which supports using declared price for the revenue estimate, but 40 of 14244 listings is a sample, not a census.",
    "The single DRIFT row is plausibly legitimate parameter-dependent pricing, not a confirmed misquote.",
    "The probe reads only accepts[0] of the 402 challenge; a decoy-then-real-price pattern in a later accepts entry would read as a false MATCH and was not checked for.",
    "About 61 percent of listings that returned a 402 in this sample carried the challenge in a response header, not the body; a body-only parser misreads most of the live market as unparseable.",
    "Only Base-mainnet USDC listings priced at 100 USD or less are counted; other chains and outlier junk listings (one priced at ten billion dollars) are excluded."
